# Loading Skeletons

Every page or component that fetches API data must show a **layout-matched skeleton** on initial load — never blank content, `"Loading…"` text, or placeholder `"—"` values.

## When to show skeletons

| State | UI |
|-------|-----|
| Initial load (`loading && !data`) | Full page skeleton — early return before real content |
| Background refresh (privacy unlock, refetch) | Keep content visible; show inline `"Updating…"` or overlay skeleton on the changing section |
| Pagination / partial reload | Overlay skeleton on the affected section (table, list) |

Use `useLayoutEffect` to set `loading = true` (and clear stale data) **before paint** when fetch triggers change — e.g. `privacyVersion`, route mount, household switch — so users never flash stale content between navigations.

## Building blocks

Reuse primitives from `@/components/shared/page-skeletons`:

- `PageHeaderSkeleton`, `StatCardSkeleton`, `StatCardsSkeleton`
- `TableSkeleton`, `ChartCardSkeleton`, `SummaryCardSkeleton`
- `AccountTileSkeleton`, `ConnectionCardSkeleton`, `FormPanelSkeleton`

Add a page-specific skeleton (e.g. `DashboardPageSkeleton`) when a route has a distinct layout. Compose from primitives — do not duplicate pulse markup. Match the real layout: same grid columns, Card wrappers, tab controls, pie+legend pairs, and table column counts.

Base primitive: `@/components/ui/skeleton` (`animate-pulse bg-muted`).

## Page pattern

```tsx
if (loading && !data) {
  return (
    <motion.div initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 12 }} animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}>
      <MyPageSkeleton />
    </motion.div>
  );
}
```

Complex pages with custom hooks: distinguish `loading` (first fetch) from `refreshing` (background). Skeleton only on `loading && !plan`.

## Do not

- Use `"Loading…"` text as the primary loading indicator on pages
- Show stat cards or tables with empty/`"—"` values while fetching
- Use spinners for full-page loads (spinners are for buttons and inline actions)
- Add Next.js `loading.tsx` for API-bound client pages — skeletons live in the page component

## New pages checklist

1. Create or reuse a page skeleton matching the final layout
2. Early-return skeleton when `loading && !data`
3. Handle background refresh without replacing the whole page
4. Use `TableSkeleton` overlay for paginated tables
